  "uses_raw": true,
  "prompt": "Which subscriptions have events that arrived twice, and by how much is each one's event count inflated? These tables may hold errors. Some subscription events arrived twice: two rows of subscription_events are copies of one event when subscription_id, event_type, event_date and mrr_delta_local all match. Keep the row with the lowest event_id. Clean nothing else. Return three columns, in this order: subscription_id, rows_arrived (all of the subscription's rows) and events (its events once copies are removed). Return one row for each subscription with at least one copy. Any row order is fine.",
